# Copy to deploy/.env (compose reads the .env beside compose.yaml) and fill in. These
# are not secrets; the secrets go in runner.env and agent.env (mode 600) in the secrets
# folder, /srv/narration unless NARRATION_SECRETS_DIR names another.
#
# The Mac's tailnet address, from `tailscale ip -4` on the Mac. An address rather than a
# name: the firewall makes its grant when the container starts, and a tailnet name may
# not resolve inside a container. The narration server accepts it as a Host header
# (NARRATION_ALLOWED_HOSTS in its plist lists TAILNET_IP:8770).
MAC_HOST=
# The narration server's port, NARRATION_PORT in the Mac's plist.
MAC_PORT=8770
# Hostnames the runner may reach on any port, comma-separated: the source site and the
# ntfy host (the host in NTFY_TOPIC_URL), plus Audiobookshelf if AUDIOBOOKSHELF_URL names
# it by hostname. For example: www.thenewatlantis.com,ntfy.sh
RUNNER_ALLOW=
# More host:port grants for the runner, comma-separated, besides the Mac's (which comes
# from MAC_HOST and MAC_PORT): Audiobookshelf when AUDIOBOOKSHELF_URL names it by
# address. For example: 192.168.1.20:13378. Empty when there is nothing to add.
RUNNER_LAN=
# The folder holding runner.env and agent.env. Empty means /srv/narration. Docker's
# snap package can't read /srv: there, use a folder under /root, such as /root/narration
# (mode 700) (docs/pipeline.md, "Docker from the snap package").
NARRATION_SECRETS_DIR=
